      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary logic supporting congestion pricing is that it directly addresses the high **unseen cost of traffic congestion** in a thriving city.\n\nBy charging a fee for driving in the most central, most valuable areas, it encourages a **demand shift** to more efficient alternatives like subways, public transit, or off-peak driving.\n\nThis dedicated revenue is then often used to **subsidize and improve the very public transit** the policy is designed to support, creating a self-funding, better system for the whole population.",
